## DEFINITION
UniProt (Universal Protein Resource) is a comprehensive protein database that provides protein sequences, functional information, and annotations.

## PURPOSE
- Store protein sequence and functional data.
- Provide curated protein annotations.
- Support protein identification and analysis.
- Facilitate biological and biomedical research.

## FEATURES
- Reviewed (Swiss-Prot) and unreviewed (TrEMBL) entries.
- Functional, structural, and sequence information.
- Cross-references to other biological databases.
- Advanced search and analysis tools.

## COMMON USES
- Protein function prediction.
- Protein sequence retrieval.
- Homology and evolutionary studies.
- Functional annotation of proteins.

## FILE TYPES
- FASTA (.fasta, .fa)
- TXT (.txt)
- XML (.xml)
- RDF (.rdf)
- GFF (.gff)

## FILES TO UPLOAD
- Protein FASTA (.fasta, .fa)
- Protein sequence (.txt)
- UniProt accession ID or protein name

## IMPORTANT POINTS
- Contains both reviewed (Swiss-Prot) and unreviewed (TrEMBL) records.
- One of the largest and most reliable protein databases.
- Integrates data from multiple biological resources.
- Freely accessible for research and education.
